{
	"Name": "AlertQuery - Okta - System / User - Recovery - High Number of Okta Password Reset or Unlock Attempts [table]",
	"Description": "Counts the self-service recovery messages Okta sent per account: password reset and account unlock mail, SMS, and voice calls, plus the recovery tokens it issued. Account recovery is the standard way around MFA, so a burst against one account is someone working the recovery flow rather than the password.\n\nThreshold: 3 or more recovery messages per account. Edit the eval near the end of the query to tune it.\n\nThis detection uses stats, so it renders as a table rather than shipping raw entries.\n\nReference(s):\n- https://support.okta.com/help/s/article/User-Signin-and-Recovery-Events-in-the-Okta-System-Log\n- https://developer.okta.com/docs/reference/api/event-types/",
	"GUID": "0d044dee-b02f-5434-b7da-3511c010c0e0",
	"Labels": [
